# Zappy mobile — environment configuration (C8)
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local work. Expo inlines any variable prefixed with
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ into the bundle at build time, so NOTHING SECRET goes here — the
# app only ever carries public, client-safe configuration (SECURITY.md).
#
# Secrets that must NEVER appear in this file or the app:
#   JWT secrets · MongoDB/Redis credentials · Cashfree or Razorpay secret keys
#   AWS keys · Firebase admin service-account credentials
#
# For staging/production these are supplied as EAS build environment variables
# rather than committed files.

# ── Which environment this bundle represents ────────────────────────────────
# development | staging | production
EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development

# ── API origin (NO trailing slash, NO /api suffix) ──────────────────────────
# Development: leave UNSET. The app derives the API host from the Expo dev
# server address, so a physical device on the same Wi-Fi works with no edits.
# Set it only to point at a non-default host.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.10:4000
#
# Staging:    EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://staging-api.zappyone.com
# Production: EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.zappyone.com
#
# REQUIRED for staging and production — the app throws at startup if a
# non-development build has no API URL, rather than silently shipping a bundle
# that points at localhost.

# ── Network ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Request timeout in milliseconds. Default 20000.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
